{
  "id": "liGKmzyJQMs",
  "segments": [
    {
      "start": 0.24,
      "end": 8.72,
      "lines": [
        {
          "text": "Can I have everyone's attention, please?",
          "start": 0.24,
          "end": 2.2
        },
        {
          "text": "I feel so lucky celebrating with the best damn family any man could hope for.",
          "start": 3.92,
          "end": 8.72
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "start": 9,
      "end": 11.52,
      "lines": [
        {
          "text": "Dad And Fig.",
          "start": 9,
          "end": 10.68
        },
        {
          "text": "Hey, all.",
          "start": 10.88,
          "end": 11.52
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "start": 12.32,
      "end": 22.32,
      "lines": [
        {
          "text": "Gloria and I have been talking about this for a while, what with Joe getting older, I feel it's just the right time to start a new chapter. Which is why I've decided to retire.",
          "start": 12.32,
          "end": 20.88
        },
        {
          "text": "- Oh my gosh. - Oh my gosh.",
          "start": 21.24,
          "end": 22.32
        }
      ],
      "glossary": [
        {
          "term": "what with",
          "ko": "~ 등으로 인해, ~ 때문에",
          "type": "phrase"
        },
        {
          "term": "start a new chapter",
          "ko": "인생의 새로운 장을 열다",
          "type": "idiom"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "start": 22.64,
      "end": 27.68,
      "lines": [
        {
          "text": "Or maybe retired, the wrong word.",
          "start": 22.64,
          "end": 24.16
        },
        {
          "text": "More of a transition. So when people ask, Where's Jay Pritchett?",
          "start": 24.16,
          "end": 27.68
        }
      ],
      "glossary": [
        {
          "term": "transition",
          "ko": "(은퇴가 아니라) 전환, 옮겨감",
          "type": "word"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "start": 27.72,
      "end": 32.64,
      "lines": [
        {
          "text": "You tell him he's transitioning.",
          "start": 27.72,
          "end": 29.32
        },
        {
          "text": "Okay, I heard it, too. Let's go back to retiring.",
          "start": 30.12,
          "end": 32.64
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "start": 32.68,
      "end": 42.4,
      "lines": [
        {
          "text": "Hey, we can finally rent that RV and visit all the major league ballparks.",
          "start": 32.68,
          "end": 36.56
        },
        {
          "text": "Probably go ahead and do that alone. Anyway, I had to ask myself, who's the best person to lead the company?",
          "start": 36.64,
          "end": 42.4
        }
      ],
      "glossary": [
        {
          "term": "RV",
          "ko": "캠핑카 (recreational vehicle)",
          "type": "word"
        },
        {
          "term": "ballparks",
          "ko": "야구장",
          "type": "word"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "start": 43,
      "end": 46.25,
      "lines": [
        {
          "text": "And the answer is obvious.",
          "start": 43,
          "end": 44.29
        },
        {
          "text": "Chuck Feeney.",
          "start": 45.54,
          "end": 46.25
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "start": 46.54,
      "end": 55.08,
      "lines": [
        {
          "text": "Who?",
          "start": 46.54,
          "end": 47.04
        },
        {
          "text": "Gutters and screen hot shot out of Chicago. With him in charge, we can all relax knowing that the company is in good hands.",
          "start": 47.74,
          "end": 55.08
        }
      ],
      "glossary": [
        {
          "term": "hot shot",
          "ko": "잘나가는 실력자, 거물",
          "type": "idiom"
        },
        {
          "term": "in good hands",
          "ko": "안심하고 맡길 수 있는",
          "type": "idiom"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "start": 55.12,
      "end": 61.66,
      "lines": [
        {
          "text": "Claire gets a great new boss, and you all get to spend more time with yours truly.",
          "start": 55.12,
          "end": 58.92
        },
        {
          "text": "Well, to this one's new boss.",
          "start": 59.16,
          "end": 61.66
        }
      ],
      "glossary": [
        {
          "term": "yours truly",
          "ko": "(익살스럽게) 이 몸, 나 자신",
          "type": "idiom"
        },
        {
          "term": "corner office",
          "ko": "임원실, 고위직의 상징인 사무실",
          "type": "phrase"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "start": 62.75,
      "end": 70.28,
      "lines": [
        {
          "text": "Claire, that's my gesturing hand. I need it for work.",
          "start": 62.75,
          "end": 64.92
        },
        {
          "text": "I work 60 hour weeks, so Chuck Feeney could have the corner office in the best table at Closet Con.",
          "start": 66,
          "end": 70.28
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "start": 70.32,
      "end": 75.52,
      "lines": [
        {
          "text": "Honey, you need to slow down. This coat isn't quite broken in yet.",
          "start": 70.32,
          "end": 72.86
        },
        {
          "text": "Listen, you have every right to be mad.",
          "start": 73.43,
          "end": 75.52
        }
      ],
      "glossary": [
        {
          "term": "broken in",
          "ko": "(옷·신발을) 길들인",
          "type": "phrase"
        },
        {
          "term": "every right to be mad",
          "ko": "화낼 만한 충분한 이유",
          "type": "phrase"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "start": 75.64,
      "end": 81.68,
      "lines": [
        {
          "text": "Everyone knows you deserve that job.",
          "start": 75.64,
          "end": 77.6
        },
        {
          "text": "Think of all the weekends I worked and the family vacations we put off.",
          "start": 78.12,
          "end": 81.68
        }
      ],
      "glossary": [
        {
          "term": "put off",
          "ko": "미루다, 연기하다",
          "type": "phrase"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "start": 81.68,
      "end": 84.87,
      "lines": [
        {
          "text": "Not to mention the stress and the insomnia.",
          "start": 81.68,
          "end": 84.12
        },
        {
          "text": "Come here.",
          "start": 84.16,
          "end": 84.87
        }
      ],
      "glossary": [
        {
          "term": "insomnia",
          "ko": "불면증",
          "type": "word"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "start": 86.5,
      "end": 95.64,
      "lines": [
        {
          "text": "Claire, life's like a mountain road with a new adventure around every corner.",
          "start": 86.5,
          "end": 92.12
        },
        {
          "text": "If that's the slogan this stupid coat, I'm gonna kill you! - Get in here.",
          "start": 92.68,
          "end": 95.64
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "start": 98.84,
      "end": 100.44,
      "lines": [
        {
          "text": "Have you seen Claire?",
          "start": 98.84,
          "end": 99.88
        },
        {
          "text": "No.",
          "start": 99.91,
          "end": 100.44
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "start": 100.44,
      "end": 104.38,
      "lines": [
        {
          "text": "I told you this Chuck Feeney thing was a terrible idea.",
          "start": 100.44,
          "end": 103.32
        },
        {
          "text": "It's a brilliant idea.",
          "start": 103.36,
          "end": 104.38
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "start": 104.78,
      "end": 112.96,
      "lines": [
        {
          "text": "There is no Chuck Feeney I made him up because of what happened to Don McSorley when he turned his company over to his son.",
          "start": 104.78,
          "end": 110.2
        },
        {
          "text": "Son only took the job because he felt obligated.",
          "start": 110.84,
          "end": 112.96
        }
      ],
      "glossary": [
        {
          "term": "made him up",
          "ko": "(인물·이야기를) 지어냈다",
          "type": "phrase"
        },
        {
          "term": "turned ... over to",
          "ko": "~에게 넘기다, 양도하다",
          "type": "phrase"
        },
        {
          "term": "obligated",
          "ko": "의무감을 느끼는",
          "type": "word"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "start": 113.52,
      "end": 118.4,
      "lines": [
        {
          "text": "One year later, business went bankrupt.",
          "start": 113.52,
          "end": 115.64
        },
        {
          "text": "Broke my heart to buy his entire inventory.",
          "start": 116.44,
          "end": 118.4
        }
      ],
      "glossary": [
        {
          "term": "went bankrupt",
          "ko": "파산했다",
          "type": "phrase"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "start": 118.72,
      "end": 122.2,
      "lines": [
        {
          "text": "8 cents on the dollar.",
          "start": 118.72,
          "end": 119.9
        },
        {
          "text": "I'm doing this for Claire.",
          "start": 121.03,
          "end": 122.2
        }
      ],
      "glossary": [
        {
          "term": "cents on the dollar",
          "ko": "1달러당 몇 센트, 즉 헐값에",
          "type": "idiom"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "start": 122.24,
      "end": 127.48,
      "lines": [
        {
          "text": "She'd do anything to make me happy. And that's not why I want her to take the job.",
          "start": 122.24,
          "end": 125.76
        },
        {
          "text": "If she wants it, she'll fight for it.",
          "start": 125.76,
          "end": 127.48
        }
      ],
      "glossary": [
        {
          "term": "easy out",
          "ko": "손쉽게 빠져나갈 구실",
          "type": "idiom"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "start": 127.52,
      "end": 131.25,
      "lines": [
        {
          "text": "If not, I just gave her an easy out.",
          "start": 127.52,
          "end": 129.12
        },
        {
          "text": "I can think of ten better ways to do this.",
          "start": 129.12,
          "end": 131.25
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "start": 131.29,
      "end": 134.73,
      "lines": [
        {
          "text": "Relax. It's going to be perfect.",
          "start": 131.29,
          "end": 133.01
        },
        {
          "text": "She'll come to me. Demand what's hers.",
          "start": 133.01,
          "end": 134.73
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "start": 134.73,
      "end": 137.81,
      "lines": [
        {
          "text": "I'll tell her the truth. Big hug. Perfect Christmas.",
          "start": 134.73,
          "end": 137.05
        },
        {
          "text": "I'm a genius.",
          "start": 137.05,
          "end": 137.81
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "start": 137.85,
      "end": 142.91,
      "lines": [
        {
          "text": "You're a crazy person.",
          "start": 137.85,
          "end": 138.87
        },
        {
          "text": "In my village, we will tie a tin can around your neck to know when you're coming.",
          "start": 138.87,
          "end": 142.91
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "start": 144.01,
      "end": 148.09,
      "lines": [
        {
          "text": "There she is. Haven't seen you since my big announcement.",
          "start": 144.01,
          "end": 147.05
        },
        {
          "text": "What do you think?",
          "start": 147.29,
          "end": 148.09
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "start": 148.13,
      "end": 155.49,
      "lines": [
        {
          "text": "I think that I gave my all to this company.",
          "start": 148.13,
          "end": 150.09
        },
        {
          "text": "And that if you were going to hand over the reins to somebody, it should be me and not some hump from Chicago.",
          "start": 150.09,
          "end": 155.49
        }
      ],
      "glossary": [
        {
          "term": "hand over the reins",
          "ko": "실권·통제권을 넘기다",
          "type": "idiom"
        },
        {
          "term": "hump",
          "ko": "(속어) 별 볼 일 없는 놈",
          "type": "word"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "start": 155.53,
      "end": 158.39,
      "lines": [
        {
          "text": "Well, it just so happens.",
          "start": 155.53,
          "end": 157.17
        },
        {
          "text": "I'm not finished Dad.",
          "start": 157.21,
          "end": 158.39
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "start": 158.76,
      "end": 165.66,
      "lines": [
        {
          "text": "Thank you for saving me from wasting the next 20 years of my life.",
          "start": 158.76,
          "end": 162.13
        },
        {
          "text": "Talking about slats, rods and hinges.",
          "start": 162.17,
          "end": 165.66
        }
      ],
      "glossary": [
        {
          "term": "hinges",
          "ko": "경첩",
          "type": "word"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "start": 165.66,
      "end": 170.65,
      "lines": [
        {
          "text": "From becoming the most boring person in the most boring industry on earth.",
          "start": 165.66,
          "end": 169.65
        },
        {
          "text": "- Boring? - Boring!",
          "start": 169.69,
          "end": 170.65
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "start": 170.69,
      "end": 175.55,
      "lines": [
        {
          "text": "Closets bring order to a chaotic world.",
          "start": 170.69,
          "end": 173.13
        },
        {
          "text": "What happened?",
          "start": 175.05,
          "end": 175.55
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "start": 175.57,
      "end": 179.81,
      "lines": [
        {
          "text": "Tell you what happened. I raised a mean, ungrateful daughter.",
          "start": 175.57,
          "end": 177.8
        },
        {
          "text": "And I'm glad I gave the business to Chuck Feeney.",
          "start": 177.8,
          "end": 179.81
        }
      ],
      "glossary": [
        {
          "term": "ungrateful",
          "ko": "배은망덕한, 은혜를 모르는",
          "type": "word"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "start": 179.89,
      "end": 181.73,
      "lines": [
        {
          "text": "There is no Chuck Feeney.",
          "start": 179.89,
          "end": 181.73
        }
      ]
    }
  ]
}
